 on the character  what could cause her to be so ostracized  from her professional community and  create all this hostility that she  eventually unleashes on diana  despite diana's attempts to befriend her  a slightly less subtle small detail  present are the parallels between  young diana prince and adult diana  prince  it happens right at the trailer's outset  as young diana is participating in the  amazon games alongside her sisters  we watch as the tiny warrior sprints  with all her might  surpassing her competitors with an  expression of determination on her face  that's spliced with footage of adult  diana racing down a city street  making the exact same face her younger  self did all those years ago  then as kid diana bolts up the curved  edges of the oval amphitheater pumping  her  arms through the air and finally leaping  into the open air beyond the dome  we see adult diana slicing the city air  with her gauntleted arms and then  swinging her lasso of truth before  flinging herself into space it's a  compelling bit of parallelism and  possibly hints that wonder woman 1984  will be digging deeper into diana's  upbringing to show how she became the  superhero she is today  you're stronger than you believe you  have greater powers than you know  it seems that somewhere in the course of  the movie maxwell lord will basically  wish himself into the white house with  the mysterious artifact that gives  barbara her powers  and lets diana have her long lost love  steve trevor back  in the first trailer for the film lord's  big overture to the world about giving  them what they want is  filmed over a diamond themed background  in another scene from the trailer we see  magical gusts buffeting the artifact as  lord performs  some supernatural act perhaps he grants  the whole world's wishes to gain  legitimacy as president  the new trailer includes lord's speech  as well but the broadcast takes place  over several computer monitors  and plays out over the airwaves as 